/* 
LeetCode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/project-employees-i/

Problem Name: Average Experience Years of Employees per Project

Beginner-Friendly Explanation:
We need to find the average years of experience of employees working on each project.
- "Project" table shows which employees belong to which project.
- "Employee" table gives experience_years for each employee.
We combine both, then calculate average experience per project.

Step-by-Step Approach:
1. Join Project and Employee on employee_id.
2. Group results by project_id (since we want per project).
3. Use AVG(experience_years) to get the mean.
4. Round to 2 decimal places using ROUND().

Why JOIN is used:
- Project only has employee_id, not experience.
- Employee has experience but no project_id.
- JOIN lets us connect both so we can calculate averages correctly.

Input Example:
Project:
+-------------+-------------+
| project_id  | employee_id |
+-------------+-------------+
| 1           | 1           |
| 1           | 2           |
| 1           | 3           |
| 2           | 1           |
| 2           | 4           |
+-------------+-------------+

Employee:
+-------------+--------+------------------+
| employee_id | name   | experience_years |
+-------------+--------+------------------+
| 1           | Khaled | 3                |
| 2           | Ali    | 2                |
| 3           | John   | 1                |
| 4           | Doe    | 2                |
+-------------+--------+------------------+

Output:
+-------------+---------------+
| project_id  | average_years |
+-------------+---------------+
| 1           | 2.00          |
| 2           | 2.50          |
+-------------+---------------+

SQL Query with Explanation:
*/
SELECT a.project_id,
       ROUND(AVG(b.experience_years), 2) AS average_years
FROM Project AS a
JOIN Employee AS b
  ON a.employee_id = b.employee_id   -- Join both tables to connect project with employee experience
GROUP BY a.project_id;               -- Group by project to calculate average per project
